  "conclusions": [
    {
      "text": "Every one of the 78 scoped source IDs/name labels occurs exactly once in the retained 145-feature geoBoundaries file and has a unique 2017/current SORS name/code and parent roster match; current explicit type agrees with all Atlas City/Municipality labels. This is a candidate register crosswalk, not polygon identity.",
      "status": "supported",
      "source_ids": [
        "geoboundaries-srb-adm2",
        "sors-cities-2017",
        "sors-cities-current"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "All current primary city/municipality codes in each of the exact 12 selected administrative districts and the City of Belgrade equal the 78 scoped Atlas codes (13/13 partitions).",
      "status": "supported",
      "source_ids": [
        "sors-cities-current",
        "sors-administrative-division"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The current SORS roster exposes 19 urban-municipality child rows under scoped city features Belgrade and Užice; they are not separate #998 subjects and have no Atlas-feature join in this packet.",
      "status": "supported",
      "source_ids": [
        "sors-cities-current"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The official RGA polygon register and dated version are needed to verify legal geometry, effective date, source-feature identity, exact parent polygons, and boundary completeness; these were not obtained.",
      "status": "unresolved",
      "source_ids": [
        "geoboundaries-srb-adm2",
        "rgz-administrative-units-register",
        "sors-spatial-register"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The 2017 source metadata labels boundaryYear 2017 but records 2023 source-update and build dates; effective/legal boundary vintage remains unresolved.",
      "status": "unresolved",
      "source_ids": [
        "geoboundaries-srb-adm2"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SORS lists 29 Kosovo-and-Metohija-region primary codes, outside this issue scope, while its statistical methodology reports that certain Kosovo data have not been available since 1999. These facts do not resolve territorial status, governance, or legal boundary meaning.",
      "status": "supported",
      "source_ids": [
        "sors-administrative-division",
        "sors-kosovo-statistical-method",
        "rgz-administrative-units-register"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Belgrade appears as an official city code (79014) but Atlas models it as a one-child province parent; a hierarchy owner should review the parent role without changing the existing member ID in this research packet.",
      "status": "supported",
      "source_ids": [
        "sors-cities-current",
        "rgz-administrative-units-register"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SORS states its file reuse terms permit redistribution with changed data clearly marked and SORS cited; no RGA polygon reuse license was acquired.",
      "status": "supported",
      "source_ids": [
        "sors-reuse-terms",
        "rgz-administrative-units-register"
      ]
    }
  ],
